<title>FRANCE: Paribas seen floating dog food unit - paper.</title>
<headline>Paribas seen floating dog food unit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paribas is expected to float its dog food unit Royal Canin and make a statement as soon as today, the Les Echos newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday agro-food group Sagal, controlled by Paribas, was suspended at 621 francs ahead of an expected statement. Sagal owns Royal Canin, as well as food ingredients firm Diana and prepared meals unit Soprat-Pere Dodu. It has total sales of 3.4 billion francs.</p>
<p>Les Echos said that Royal Canin would be taken out of Sagal, floated seperately, and Sagal with the other units would be permanently taken off the bourse.</p>
